    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82936" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πήλιον</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πάλιον</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], τό</span>, <u>Pelion</u>,
		a mountain in Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.757
		</span></i>, etc.:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηλιάς</span></b>  (q. v.); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηλιῶτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>on</i> or <i>at the foot of
				Pelion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				484
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηλιωτικός</span></b> ,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				154
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πηλιακός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.110
			</span></i>.</div>
